e-defining-features-jaishankar-decodes-the-changing-world-order/articleshow/135963686.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135963686.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During his speech in Japan, S Jaishankar highlighted concerns about the weaponization of the global economy, noting key trends that are redefining international relationships such as strategic rivalry and resource manipulation. He stressed the necessity for trustworthy alliances and diversification amid economic uncertainties. Jaishankar further advocated for deepened collaboration between India and Japan across multiple sectors, as this could foster enhanced stability in the Indo-Pacific region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/five-defining-features-jaishankar-decodes-the-changing-world-order/articleshow/135963686.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/five-defining-features-jaishankar-decodes-the-changing-world-order/articleshow/135963686.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-18T18:12:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135963741,imgsize-79928.cms"/></item></channel></rss>